1
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:57,550
Oh, my God.

2
00:04:57,710 --> 00:04:59,590
Are you okay?

3
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:02,840
Do you want me to call 911?

4
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:08,890
What are you-?

5
00:06:12,750 --> 00:06:15,250
You, in the silver Lexus. Slow down.

6
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:17,750
Slow down and pull over immediately.

7
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:34,270
Lady, have you any idea 
how fast you were going?

8
00:06:34,430 --> 00:06:36,390
Let me see your license and registration.

9
00:06:39,860 --> 00:06:43,400
- Okay, what have we got? 
- This new computer virus is tricky.

10
00:06:43,690 --> 00:06:47,280
It's infected half the civilian Internet 
as well as secondary military apps.

11
00:06:47,450 --> 00:06:50,240
- Payroll, inventory. 
- Primary defense nets are still clean?

12
00:06:50,530 --> 00:06:52,660
So far the firewalls are holding up.

13
00:06:52,910 --> 00:06:56,620
Sir, the Pentagon has proposed we use 
our Al to scan the infrastructure.

14
00:06:56,790 --> 00:06:59,250
Search and destroy 
for any hint of the virus.

15
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:02,750
I know, Tony, but that's like 
going after a fly with a bazooka.

16
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:05,550
Once the connection's made, 
it should only be a few minutes.

17
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:10,100
During which we've put everything under 
the control of a single computer system.

18
00:07:10,260 --> 00:07:13,060
The most intelligent system 
ever conceived.

19
00:07:13,220 --> 00:07:16,230
I still prefer to keep humans in the loop.

20
00:07:16,350 --> 00:07:18,520
I'm not sure Skynet's ready.

21
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:20,610
Yes, sir.

22
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:56,160
Thanks.

23
00:11:04,290 --> 00:11:06,080
Welcome to Jim's Burgers. 
Can I take your order?

24
00:11:07,290 --> 00:11:11,000
- Jose Barrera? 
- Yeah, that's me.

25
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:33,190
Growing concern over widespread outages 
in the global digital network...

26
00:11:33,480 --> 00:11:36,820
...have prompted rumors 
of a new computer super-virus.

27
00:11:36,990 --> 00:11:40,530
- Wall Street analysts are confident... 
- Shit! My mom's home.

28
00:11:40,990 --> 00:11:43,790
Here. Hide the beer. Hide the beer. 
Here. Take that.

29
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:46,870
Go, go, go.

30
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:55,460
Elizabeth and William Anderson?

31
00:11:56,170 --> 00:12:00,590
I'm Bill. My sister's upstairs. 
Is there something wrong?

32
00:12:13,610 --> 00:12:15,230
What's going on?

33
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:18,610
I have to go to the clinic. 
It's an emergency.

34
00:12:18,950 --> 00:12:20,950
It's 4:30 in the morning.

35
00:12:21,450 --> 00:12:24,870
Well, I'll be back before you get up.

36
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:10,830
Cool it, guys, it's just me.

37
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:14,420
We've got a sick cat coming in.

38
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:43,450
Please, don't do that.

39
00:13:47,330 --> 00:13:49,700
I suppose it was you who 
ripped us off last week.

40
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:52,710
Put the phone down.

41
00:13:53,830 --> 00:13:55,790
Sorry.

42
00:13:56,130 --> 00:13:57,670
I just...

43
00:13:57,840 --> 00:13:59,960
I needed some medicine.

44
00:14:00,130 --> 00:14:03,720
There's an emergency clinic 
half a mile away.

45
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:05,470
Can't do that.

46
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:12,980
How much did you take?

47
00:14:13,140 --> 00:14:14,890
- Enough. 
- Well...

48
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:18,730
...this is the stuff we use 
to chemically neuter dogs.

49
00:14:21,530 --> 00:14:23,030
Take a look.

50
00:14:24,990 --> 00:14:26,360
Hey!

51
00:14:31,830 --> 00:14:34,040
Jesus! You didn't have to do that!

52
00:14:34,870 --> 00:14:37,380
Next time bring a clue, 
not a paintball gun.

53
00:14:37,540 --> 00:14:41,050
- No, this isn't what you think. 
- Yeah, right.

54
00:15:21,710 --> 00:15:23,420
You're John Connor.

55
00:15:27,930 --> 00:15:31,180
I'm Kate Brewster.

56
00:15:34,060 --> 00:15:36,680
We went to 
West Hills Junior High together.

57
00:15:41,230 --> 00:15:44,360
- Jesus. 
- What happened to you, John?

58
00:15:44,730 --> 00:15:48,660
Middle of eighth grade, 
you just disappeared.

59
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:52,160
And there was that thing 
about your foster parents.

60
00:15:52,410 --> 00:15:55,040
Yeah, they were murdered.

61
00:15:56,830 --> 00:15:59,540
I didn't do it.

62
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:03,000
What the hell?

63
00:16:03,210 --> 00:16:05,800
Is somebody with you?

64
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:29,700
Katherine Brewster?

65
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:47,920
No.

66
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:40,830
John Connor was here. 
Where did he go?

67
00:18:41,580 --> 00:18:44,290
Tell me. Where did he go?

68
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:25,500
Katherine Brewster?

69
00:19:30,290 --> 00:19:32,750
What are you doing? Let me down!

70
00:19:33,130 --> 00:19:36,340
Let me down! Let me down!

71
00:19:38,590 --> 00:19:40,180
Where is John Connor?

72
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:43,470
He's...

73
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:46,810
...in the kennel, in a cage.

74
00:19:50,650 --> 00:19:56,070
Please, please, please. 
You have to let me go!

75
00:20:43,870 --> 00:20:46,910
John Connor.

76
00:20:48,540 --> 00:20:51,250
It is time.

77
00:20:52,120 --> 00:20:54,880
You here to kill me?

78
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:03,760
No. You must live.

79
00:21:14,560 --> 00:21:18,400
- Why are you here? Where are we going? 
- Keep moving.

80
00:21:21,150 --> 00:21:23,450
Get out of here.

81
00:21:24,570 --> 00:21:26,280
Now!

82
00:22:15,120 --> 00:22:17,630
- No pulse. 
- See if you can get him down.

83
00:22:19,300 --> 00:22:21,170
I can't.

84
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:23,340
This guy weighs a ton.

85
00:22:47,820 --> 00:22:51,120
- 911. 
- Yes. Yes. I'm being kidnapped.

86
00:22:51,290 --> 00:22:54,830
- Where are you now? 
- I don't know where. I'm in my truck.

87
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:57,500
It's a Toyota Tundra.

88
00:22:57,830 --> 00:23:03,090
It says "Emery Animal Hospital" 
on the side. I'm locked inside the back.

89
00:23:04,170 --> 00:23:05,510
Hello?

90
00:23:06,380 --> 00:23:08,720
Hello?

91
00:23:11,180 --> 00:23:13,430
Shit! Shit!

92
00:24:27,300 --> 00:24:28,970
Get off.

93
00:24:45,190 --> 00:24:46,150
Let me out!

94
00:24:46,570 --> 00:24:48,030
What are you doing here?

95
00:24:48,190 --> 00:24:50,740
You tell me. You got me into this.

96
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:53,410
- Stop the car. 
- I can't. Not yet.

97
00:24:53,570 --> 00:24:57,620
- You bastard! Stop the car! 
- Shut up!

98
00:25:09,220 --> 00:25:11,630
Son of a bitch.

99
00:25:12,220 --> 00:25:14,220
Goddamn it.

100
00:25:14,640 --> 00:25:16,470
What are you doing?

101
00:25:16,850 --> 00:25:19,730
If you don't have insurance, 
I'm gonna rip your balls off.

102
00:25:19,020 --> 00:25:21,350
- I don't want any problems, okay? 
- Shut up!

103
00:25:21,350 --> 00:25:25,110
- I'm being kidnapped! Call the police! 
- Well, I'll be goddamned.

104
00:25:25,270 --> 00:25:27,110
- Call 911! 
- A cop when you need one.

105
00:25:27,270 --> 00:25:29,110
Help, please! Please!

106
00:25:29,530 --> 00:25:32,110
Let me out of here! Help!

107
00:25:34,870 --> 00:25:37,580
Get back here, asshole!

108
00:26:00,220 --> 00:26:02,480
That's the cops! 
You have to pull over!

109
00:26:02,640 --> 00:26:04,270
Yeah, first chance I get.

110
00:27:09,960 --> 00:27:11,340
Hold on!

111
00:28:21,280 --> 00:28:23,490
Stop it!

112
00:29:29,220 --> 00:29:30,560
I'll drive.

113
00:29:37,360 --> 00:29:38,980
Get out.

114
00:30:35,580 --> 00:30:37,630
Excuse me.

115
00:31:21,960 --> 00:31:23,210
Move over.

116
00:31:45,860 --> 00:31:48,200
Do you even remember me?

117
00:31:49,320 --> 00:31:52,870
Sarah Connor? Blowing up Cyberdyne?

118
00:31:53,120 --> 00:31:56,410
"Hasta la vista, baby. " 
Ring any bells?

119
00:31:56,580 --> 00:31:59,080
That was a different T-101.

120
00:31:59,580 --> 00:32:01,960
What, do you come off an assembly line 
or something?

121
00:32:02,130 --> 00:32:03,340
Exactly.

122
00:32:04,170 --> 00:32:07,470
Oh, man. I'm gonna have 
to teach you everything all over again.

123
00:32:09,260 --> 00:32:12,510
Katherine Brewster, 
have you sustained injury?

124
00:32:12,890 --> 00:32:15,350
Drop dead, you asshole!

125
00:32:16,600 --> 00:32:19,060
I'm unable to comply.

126
00:32:28,320 --> 00:32:30,110
Where are you taking me?

127
00:32:30,280 --> 00:32:32,450
To a safe location.

128
00:32:49,050 --> 00:32:51,640
All right, get off at the next exit. 
Let her out.

129
00:32:51,800 --> 00:32:55,010
Negative. 
Katherine Brewster must be protected.

130
00:32:55,510 --> 00:32:58,810
- I thought I was the one they were after. 
- You could not be located.

131
00:32:59,020 --> 00:33:03,480
So a T-X was sent back through time 
to eliminate your lieutenants.

132
00:33:04,560 --> 00:33:08,490
So she's gonna be in the Resistance?

133
00:33:11,570 --> 00:33:14,830
No, no. 
No, you shouldn't even exist.

134
00:33:15,030 --> 00:33:17,540
I mean, 
we took out Cyberdyne over 10 years ago.

135
00:33:17,700 --> 00:33:21,540
- We stopped Judgment Day. 
- You only postponed it.

136
00:33:21,710 --> 00:33:23,920
Judgment Day is inevitable.

137
00:33:31,380 --> 00:33:33,430
I require a cutting tool.

138
00:33:40,350 --> 00:33:42,640
Here, take the wheel.

139
00:33:45,900 --> 00:33:49,480
- What are you doing? 
- I am powered by two hydrogen fuel cells.

140
00:33:49,650 --> 00:33:52,950
My primary cell was damaged 
by a plasma attack.

141
00:33:53,240 --> 00:33:57,240
T- X is designed for extreme combat, 
driven by a plasma reactor...

142
00:33:57,410 --> 00:33:59,370
...and equipped with onboard weapons.

143
00:33:58,660 --> 00:34:00,870
Its arsenal includes...

144
00:34:01,080 --> 00:34:03,620
...nanotechnological transjectors.

145
00:34:03,790 --> 00:34:07,670
- Meaning? 
- It can control other machines.

146
00:34:09,760 --> 00:34:14,800
Its body chassis is heavily armored 
and hardened to withstand external attack.

147
00:34:17,260 --> 00:34:19,930
My presence in this timeline 
has been anticipated.

148
00:34:20,470 --> 00:34:24,520
T- X is designed to terminate 
other cybernetic organisms.

149
00:34:41,120 --> 00:34:45,290
When ruptured, 
the fuel cells become unstable.

150
00:34:45,790 --> 00:34:47,080
Relax.

151
00:34:47,290 --> 00:34:48,500
- Let me out of here!

152
00:35:32,300 --> 00:35:33,840
Hey.

153
00:35:34,260 --> 00:35:36,760
Hey! Are you gonna pay for that?

154
00:35:41,140 --> 00:35:42,220
Talk to the hand.

155
00:35:42,220 --> 00:35:42,970
Talk to the hand.

156
00:35:59,410 --> 00:36:02,200
Help! Help me!

157
00:36:02,700 --> 00:36:04,370
Help!

158
00:36:08,080 --> 00:36:10,170
I think we better go.

159
00:36:42,240 --> 00:36:43,830
Jerky?

160
00:36:44,700 --> 00:36:46,120
You're kidnapping me.

161
00:36:47,910 --> 00:36:50,290
- Look- 
- God, you were always a delinquent.

162
00:36:50,460 --> 00:36:54,380
And look at you now, sitting there 
like the bad boy thing still works.

163
00:36:54,540 --> 00:36:57,420
What are you, 
some kind of gang member?

164
00:36:57,590 --> 00:37:00,010
How do you live with yourself?

165
00:37:02,220 --> 00:37:03,800
What?

166
00:37:08,270 --> 00:37:09,850
Tell her who I am.

167
00:37:10,060 --> 00:37:15,730
John Connor is leader of the Worldwide 
Resistance and last hope of humankind.

168
00:37:17,280 --> 00:37:19,690
Right. And him?

169
00:37:20,700 --> 00:37:23,110
He's a robot from the future.

170
00:37:23,280 --> 00:37:26,950
Living tissue over a metal skeleton, 
sent back in time to protect me.

171
00:37:27,120 --> 00:37:28,910
Go to hell.

172
00:37:29,660 --> 00:37:32,250
He doesn't mean you any harm.

173
00:37:48,600 --> 00:37:51,850
Hi, I'm Detective Edwards, L.A.P.D. 
This is Detective Bell.

174
00:37:51,690 --> 00:37:55,190
We're looking for Katherine Brewster. 
Is she here?

175
00:37:55,360 --> 00:37:56,560
No.

176
00:37:56,730 --> 00:38:01,110
- You're her fiance, Scott Mason? 
- Yes.

177
00:38:01,320 --> 00:38:05,160
There was an incident at the 
veterinary hospital where she works.

178
00:38:05,320 --> 00:38:08,030
We're concerned something 
may have happened to her.

179
00:38:08,200 --> 00:38:09,370
Where is she?

180
00:38:09,620 --> 00:38:12,080
We got a report from a gas station 
attendant near Victorville...

181
00:38:13,160 --> 00:38:17,090
...about a possible kidnapping 
and it might be related.

182
00:38:17,250 --> 00:38:19,550
I'll help you find her.

183
00:38:31,560 --> 00:38:33,270
Come with me.

184
00:38:37,860 --> 00:38:39,320
Go.

185
00:39:07,300 --> 00:39:08,930
Your mother?

186
00:39:11,430 --> 00:39:14,390
I never even knew 
where she was buried.

187
00:39:17,310 --> 00:39:20,190
I hit the road the day she died.

188
00:39:24,070 --> 00:39:26,360
Why did you bring me here?

189
00:39:30,330 --> 00:39:31,790
No! What are you doing?

190
00:39:31,950 --> 00:39:33,500
Hey, stop!

191
00:39:33,750 --> 00:39:35,040
Get away from it! Stop!

192
00:39:42,750 --> 00:39:45,300
Sarah Connor was cremated in Mexico.

193
00:39:45,470 --> 00:39:47,760
Her friends scattered her ashes 
in the sea.

194
00:39:48,130 --> 00:39:51,390
They stored these weapons 
in accordance with her will.

195
00:39:56,940 --> 00:39:58,980
"Every day after this one is a gift. "

196
00:39:59,190 --> 00:40:02,020
She told me, "We made it. We're free. "

197
00:40:04,860 --> 00:40:07,490
But I never really believed that.

198
00:40:10,530 --> 00:40:12,950
I guess she didn't either.

199
00:40:14,740 --> 00:40:18,460
You know you were about 
the closest thing to a father I ever had?

200
00:40:19,620 --> 00:40:21,420
How pathetic is that?

201
00:40:22,960 --> 00:40:24,170
Out of my way!

202
00:40:27,550 --> 00:40:29,550
My mission is to protect you.

203
00:40:30,430 --> 00:40:31,720
That's enough.

204
00:40:33,300 --> 00:40:36,720
Move or I'll do it! 
I swear I will! I'll shoot you!

205
00:40:36,720 --> 00:40:40,060
Go ahead. See what happens.

206
00:40:54,830 --> 00:40:56,490
Don't do that.

207
00:40:58,580 --> 00:41:00,620
Oh, my God.

208
00:41:06,750 --> 00:41:10,090
This is the police. 
We have the building surrounded.

209
00:41:10,260 --> 00:41:12,430
Release your hostage!

210
00:41:33,820 --> 00:41:35,870
Perps still holed up?

211
00:41:36,990 --> 00:41:38,080
Gotcha.

212
00:41:38,240 --> 00:41:40,790
Good news. Your fiancee's okay.

213
00:41:40,960 --> 00:41:42,040
Where is she?

214
00:41:42,210 --> 00:41:44,710
Greenlawn Cemetery, 
up off the 5 freeway.

215
00:41:44,920 --> 00:41:48,880
It's right by the desert. 
But they're gonna bring her back to the-

216
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:52,300
Oh, my God! Oh, my dear Jesus! God!

217
00:42:16,160 --> 00:42:19,620
You're safe now. They can't hurt you.

218
00:42:20,200 --> 00:42:23,370
Kate, my name is Dr. Silberman.

219
00:42:23,540 --> 00:42:26,880
I'm a post-trauma counselor 
for the sheriff's department.

220
00:42:27,040 --> 00:42:29,050
How are you feeling?

221
00:42:29,840 --> 00:42:31,840
He's not human.

222
00:42:32,170 --> 00:42:36,340
He's really not human.

223
00:42:38,760 --> 00:42:42,230
I know what it's like to be 
in a hostage situation.

224
00:42:42,430 --> 00:42:44,480
I've been there myself.

225
00:42:44,640 --> 00:42:47,770
The fear, the adrenaline.

226
00:42:47,940 --> 00:42:51,860
You find yourself imagining things.

227
00:42:52,400 --> 00:42:54,950
Impossible things.

228
00:42:55,660 --> 00:42:57,870
Crazy things.

229
00:42:59,120 --> 00:43:01,370
Insane things.

230
00:43:03,330 --> 00:43:06,210
Take years to get over it.

231
00:43:07,460 --> 00:43:09,880
- Go, go, go! 
- Move it!

232
00:43:15,550 --> 00:43:16,840
Drop your weapon!

233
00:43:20,640 --> 00:43:22,640
And the coffin!

234
00:43:24,980 --> 00:43:27,480
Take him down! Take him down!

235
00:44:08,390 --> 00:44:10,440
Resume fire!

236
00:44:17,530 --> 00:44:19,910
We must reacquire Katherine Brewster.

237
00:44:20,700 --> 00:44:23,620
Why? What makes her 
so goddamn important?

238
00:44:23,790 --> 00:44:28,120
Through her, you contact remnants of the 
military and learn how to fight Skynet...

239
00:44:28,410 --> 00:44:30,790
...forming the core 
of the Resistance.

240
00:45:29,020 --> 00:45:30,730
Get in!

241
00:45:30,890 --> 00:45:32,400
Do you want to live? Come on!

242
00:45:54,750 --> 00:45:58,130
- It was Scott! How could it be Scott? 
- Your fiance?

243
00:45:58,300 --> 00:46:02,300
The T-X is polymimetic, 
able to take the form of anything it touches.

244
00:46:03,090 --> 00:46:05,140
Your fiance is dead.

245
00:46:29,700 --> 00:46:30,750
Oh, my God!

246
00:46:36,420 --> 00:46:37,540
Do something!

247
00:47:08,570 --> 00:47:10,280
Get down.

248
00:47:32,770 --> 00:47:35,020
We need a new vehicle.

249
00:48:57,930 --> 00:48:59,480
Hey, come on.

250
00:48:59,640 --> 00:49:01,770
We gotta keep moving.

251
00:49:03,940 --> 00:49:06,530
She killed Scott because of me.

252
00:49:13,280 --> 00:49:15,580
Look, I know this won't help...

253
00:49:17,790 --> 00:49:23,380
...but sometimes things happen 
that we just can't change.

254
00:49:27,340 --> 00:49:28,880
It's not your fault.

255
00:49:38,220 --> 00:49:41,690
So this Terminatrix, how many others 
does she have on her hit list?

256
00:49:42,100 --> 00:49:46,770
Twenty-two. Anderson, Elizabeth. 
Anderson, William.

257
00:49:46,940 --> 00:49:49,690
Barrera, Jose. Brewster, Robert.

258
00:49:49,860 --> 00:49:51,150
My father?

259
00:49:51,320 --> 00:49:56,330
Having failed to acquire its primary target, 
T- X will resume its default program.

260
00:49:56,490 --> 00:50:00,580
- She's gonna kill my father too? 
- There's a high probability.

261
00:50:01,330 --> 00:50:03,670
- No. 
- Who is he? What does he do?

262
00:50:03,830 --> 00:50:08,340
He's in the Air Force. Weapon design, 
secret stuff. I don't know, exactly.

263
00:50:08,550 --> 00:50:12,300
General Robert Brewster 
is program director of CRS...

264
00:50:12,470 --> 00:50:16,390
...Cyber Research Systems, 
autonomous weapons division.

265
00:50:16,550 --> 00:50:19,470
Skynet. You're talking about Skynet.

266
00:50:19,640 --> 00:50:23,940
Skynet is one of the digital defense systems 
developed under Brewster.

267
00:50:24,100 --> 00:50:25,600
Oh, God.

268
00:50:26,020 --> 00:50:29,230
Oh, my God. Of course.

269
00:50:29,610 --> 00:50:31,070
It all makes sense now.

270
00:50:31,940 --> 00:50:35,360
If you hadn't come back when I was a kid, 
changed everything...

271
00:50:35,530 --> 00:50:39,620
...she and I would have gotten together 
then. I would have met her father.

272
00:50:39,990 --> 00:50:42,410
- Don't you see? 
- I don't understand.

273
00:50:42,580 --> 00:50:46,540
Your father. 
This is all about your father.

274
00:50:46,710 --> 00:50:51,300
He's the key. He always was. Your father 
is the one who can shut Skynet down.

275
00:50:52,720 --> 00:50:55,180
He's the only one who ever could.

276
00:50:57,050 --> 00:50:59,220
We have to get to him 
before the T-X does.

277
00:50:59,430 --> 00:51:03,930
- Negative. I cannot jeopardize my mission. 
- This is your mission, to save people!

278
00:51:04,100 --> 00:51:08,060
My mission is to ensure the survival 
of John Connor and Katherine Brewster.

279
00:51:08,810 --> 00:51:11,110
I am giving you an order.

280
00:51:11,280 --> 00:51:13,860
I am not programmed 
to follow your orders.

281
00:51:14,070 --> 00:51:17,110
- After the nuclear war, you both- 
- Nuclear war?!

282
00:51:17,280 --> 00:51:20,370
There doesn't have to be a war! 
We can stop it!

283
00:51:20,530 --> 00:51:22,750
There is insufficient time.

284
00:51:22,910 --> 00:51:27,080
The first launch sequences 
will be initiated at 6:18 p. m.

285
00:51:27,250 --> 00:51:29,000
- What, today? 
- Affirmative.

286
00:51:29,170 --> 00:51:31,880
John, what is he saying?

287
00:51:33,010 --> 00:51:35,010
Judgment Day.

288
00:51:36,380 --> 00:51:38,590
The end of the world.

289
00:51:39,970 --> 00:51:41,930
It's today, three hours from now.

290
00:51:42,390 --> 00:51:44,390
Two hours and 53 minutes.

291
00:51:44,600 --> 00:51:49,650
We must continue south into Mexico 
to escape the primary blast zones.

292
00:51:50,400 --> 00:51:53,190
No, we have to get to her dad.

293
00:51:54,860 --> 00:51:58,780
The Mojave area will sustain 
significant nuclear fallout.

294
00:51:58,950 --> 00:52:00,570
You will not survive.

295
00:52:01,410 --> 00:52:05,750
You mean we go run and hide somewhere 
in a hole while the bombs fall?

296
00:52:06,620 --> 00:52:07,080
It is your destiny.

297
00:52:09,790 --> 00:52:14,090
Please do what he says. 
You have to save my father!

298
00:52:18,300 --> 00:52:21,800
We can reach CRS 
in approximately one hour...

299
00:52:22,010 --> 00:52:24,770
...depending on traffic conditions.

300
00:52:40,570 --> 00:52:42,240
I can't get a line.

301
00:52:45,330 --> 00:52:47,160
The whole cell network is down.

302
00:52:47,330 --> 00:52:50,250
Skynet is assuming control 
over global communications...

303
00:52:50,420 --> 00:52:52,750
...in preparation for its attack.

304
00:52:52,920 --> 00:52:57,090
So if this war is between people 
and machines...

305
00:52:57,380 --> 00:52:59,630
...why are you on our side?

306
00:52:59,800 --> 00:53:03,720
The Resistance captured me 
and reprogrammed my CPU.

307
00:53:03,890 --> 00:53:07,390
I was originally designed 
for assassination missions.

308
00:53:10,350 --> 00:53:11,850
So...

309
00:53:12,190 --> 00:53:16,070
...you don't really care 
if this mission succeeds or not.

310
00:53:16,650 --> 00:53:20,610
If we get killed, 
does that mean anything to you?

311
00:53:20,780 --> 00:53:24,030
If you were to die, 
I will become useless.

312
00:53:24,200 --> 00:53:27,330
There will be no reason for me to exist.

313
00:53:33,000 --> 00:53:35,040
Thank you for doing this.

314
00:53:35,210 --> 00:53:37,210
Your gratitude is not required.

315
00:53:37,920 --> 00:53:40,340
I am programmed 
to follow your commands.

316
00:53:41,340 --> 00:53:42,720
Her commands?

317
00:53:42,890 --> 00:53:48,270
Katherine Brewster had me reactivated and 
sent through the time displacement field.

318
00:53:48,270 --> 00:53:50,270
Why didn't I send you back?

319
00:53:50,430 --> 00:53:52,730
I am not authorized 
to answer your question.

320
00:53:54,520 --> 00:53:57,980
- Why didn't he send you back? 
- He was dead.

321
00:54:02,570 --> 00:54:04,280
Well, that sucks.

322
00:54:05,200 --> 00:54:09,120
- Humans inevitably die. 
- Yeah, I know.

323
00:54:10,040 --> 00:54:12,120
So how does it-? No.

324
00:54:12,580 --> 00:54:15,380
Maybe I don't want to know.

325
00:54:16,960 --> 00:54:18,460
How does he die?

326
00:54:19,170 --> 00:54:22,970
John Connor was terminated 
on July 4th, 2032.

327
00:54:23,130 --> 00:54:27,010
I was selected for the emotional attachment 
he had for my model number...

328
00:54:27,220 --> 00:54:31,480
...due to his boyhood experiences. 
This aided in my infiltration.

329
00:54:32,430 --> 00:54:34,060
What are you saying?

330
00:54:35,850 --> 00:54:38,190
I killed you.

331
00:54:50,450 --> 00:54:55,460
This has to be a mistake. As of 1100 hours, 
all primary military systems were secure.

332
00:54:55,620 --> 00:54:59,710
They were. Only the civilian sector 
was affected. Internet, air traffic.

333
00:54:59,880 --> 00:55:02,670
Minutes ago, guidance computers 
at Vandenberg crashed.

334
00:55:02,840 --> 00:55:05,550
We thought it was an error. 
It looks like the virus.

335
00:55:05,720 --> 00:55:09,970
- Early warning in Alaska is down. 
- Satellite signals are scrambled.

336
00:55:10,140 --> 00:55:13,020
What about the missile silos, the subs?

337
00:55:14,020 --> 00:55:16,230
We've lost contact.

338
00:55:16,730 --> 00:55:20,150
You're saying this country 
is completely open to attack.

339
00:55:20,320 --> 00:55:23,150
Theoretically, we could be 
under attack already.

340
00:55:23,320 --> 00:55:28,780
Who's doing this? A foreign power 
or some computer hacker in his garage?

341
00:55:28,950 --> 00:55:31,080
We can't trace the virus 
or pin it down.

342
00:55:31,240 --> 00:55:35,370
It keeps growing and changing, 
like it has a mind of its own.

343
00:55:35,910 --> 00:55:37,670
This can't be happening.

344
00:55:37,830 --> 00:55:42,050
The Pentagon's on the secure line. 
It's the chairman.

345
00:55:45,300 --> 00:55:47,220
All right.

346
00:56:01,650 --> 00:56:03,570
Look...

347
00:56:03,940 --> 00:56:05,860
...none of this is gonna happen.

348
00:56:06,490 --> 00:56:11,910
We get to your dad, get him to pull the plug 
on Skynet. The bombs won't fall.

349
00:56:14,290 --> 00:56:17,120
He won't have to kill me someday.

350
00:56:17,870 --> 00:56:20,210
He'll never even exist.

351
00:56:21,880 --> 00:56:27,220
You and I, we can 
just go our separate ways.

352
00:56:52,740 --> 00:56:55,370
We're hoping you have a solution for us.

353
00:56:55,540 --> 00:56:59,330
I know, sir, but Skynet is not ready 
for a system-wide connection.

354
00:56:59,500 --> 00:57:02,460
That's not what your civilian 
counterparts there told me.

355
00:57:02,630 --> 00:57:04,920
They say we can stop this damn virus.

356
00:57:05,090 --> 00:57:08,590
I understand there's a certain amount 
of performance anxiety...

357
00:57:08,760 --> 00:57:12,090
...but your boys say if we plug Skynet 
into all of our systems...

358
00:57:12,260 --> 00:57:16,350
...it'll squash this thing and give me back 
control of my military.

359
00:57:16,520 --> 00:57:19,020
Mr. Chairman, I need 
to make myself very clear.

360
00:57:19,180 --> 00:57:22,600
If we uplink now, Skynet will be 
in control of your military.

361
00:57:22,770 --> 00:57:26,820
But you'll be in control of Skynet, right?

362
00:57:27,150 --> 00:57:29,280
That is correct, sir.

363
00:57:29,450 --> 00:57:30,820
Then do it.

364
00:57:30,990 --> 00:57:33,740
And Brewster, if this thing works...

365
00:57:33,910 --> 00:57:37,290
...you'll get all the funding 
you'll ever need.

366
00:57:38,250 --> 00:57:40,160
Yes, sir.

367
00:58:48,770 --> 00:58:50,400
Sir?

368
00:58:51,650 --> 00:58:53,400
Shall I?

369
00:58:54,950 --> 00:58:56,490
No.

370
00:58:57,620 --> 00:58:59,830
It's my job now.

371
00:59:14,300 --> 00:59:17,340
- Skynet Defense System activated. 
- We're in.

372
00:59:17,510 --> 00:59:20,720
We're past the firewalls, local 
defense nets, Minutemen, subs.

373
00:59:20,890 --> 00:59:25,020
Skynet's fully operational, 
processing at 60 teraflops a second.

374
00:59:25,230 --> 00:59:29,060
It should take less than a minute 
to find the virus and kill it.

375
00:59:30,190 --> 00:59:33,030
Let's pray to God this works.

376
00:59:39,280 --> 00:59:40,450
Power failure?

377
00:59:40,620 --> 00:59:42,950
No. I don't know what it is.

378
00:59:54,010 --> 00:59:56,430
What the hell is going on?

379
00:59:56,590 --> 00:59:57,630
Daddy!

380
00:59:58,180 --> 00:59:59,720
What are you doing here?

381
01:00:06,100 --> 01:00:08,900
Daddy! Get away from it!

382
01:00:12,690 --> 01:00:14,230
Watch out!

383
01:00:31,460 --> 01:00:33,380
Daddy, don't move.

384
01:00:37,760 --> 01:00:39,470
She'll be back.

385
01:00:40,140 --> 01:00:42,100
We have to shut down Skynet.

386
01:00:42,300 --> 01:00:44,930
Where's the system core? 
In this building?

387
01:00:45,100 --> 01:00:48,890
Skynet. The virus has infected Skynet.

388
01:00:49,060 --> 01:00:52,190
Skynet is the virus! 
It's why everything's falling apart!

389
01:00:52,360 --> 01:00:54,480
Skynet has become self-aware.

390
01:00:54,650 --> 01:00:58,280
In one hour it will initiate 
a massive nuclear attack on its enemy.

391
01:00:58,490 --> 01:00:59,570
What enemy?

392
01:01:00,160 --> 01:01:01,570
Us!

393
01:01:01,740 --> 01:01:03,080
Humans.

394
01:01:12,170 --> 01:01:15,460
Oh, God! It's the machines. 
They're starting to take over.

395
01:01:15,630 --> 01:01:19,090
My office, on this floor, 
we have to get there.

396
01:01:20,260 --> 01:01:22,510
The access codes are in my safe.

397
01:02:41,300 --> 01:02:45,390
- Why are they killing everyone? 
- To destroy any possible threat to Skynet.

398
01:02:44,680 --> 01:02:47,350
Which ones are the codes?

399
01:02:47,510 --> 01:02:49,350
Red envelope.

400
01:02:53,140 --> 01:02:56,980
Crystal Peak. You have 
to get to Crystal Peak.

401
01:02:57,150 --> 01:02:59,320
- What is he saying? 
- Crystal Peak.

402
01:02:59,480 --> 01:03:02,150
A hardened facility 
in the Sierra Nevada mountains.

403
01:03:02,320 --> 01:03:06,110
Fifty-two miles northeast, 
bearing 0.5 degrees.

404
01:03:06,280 --> 01:03:07,950
That's the system core?

405
01:03:08,530 --> 01:03:10,660
It's your only chance.

406
01:03:10,830 --> 01:03:15,790
You'll need a plane. The particle accelerator 
leads to the runway.

407
01:03:17,790 --> 01:03:19,590
Take care of my daughter.

408
01:03:21,960 --> 01:03:25,380
Oh, Katie, I am sorry.

409
01:03:25,550 --> 01:03:28,850
I opened Pandora's box.

410
01:03:30,010 --> 01:03:31,010
Get down!

411
01:03:47,450 --> 01:03:49,820
There's nothing you can do. Come on.

412
01:03:49,990 --> 01:03:52,080
We must go. It is not safe here.

413
01:03:52,830 --> 01:03:55,290
Kate, we have to go.

414
01:03:55,500 --> 01:03:59,170
Kate! He wanted you to come with me.

415
01:03:59,420 --> 01:04:03,550
He wanted us to shut Skynet down. 
Come on.

416
01:04:05,340 --> 01:04:06,760
Come on.

417
01:04:18,730 --> 01:04:20,360
Run!

418
01:05:54,990 --> 01:05:56,580
Let's go.

419
01:07:07,980 --> 01:07:10,820
That's it. We can follow it 
out to the runway.

420
01:07:11,030 --> 01:07:12,740
Come on.

421
01:08:23,720 --> 01:08:26,180
Oh, God. She's coming.

422
01:08:29,730 --> 01:08:31,610
What are you doing?

423
01:08:32,690 --> 01:08:33,730
Powering up.

424
01:08:38,910 --> 01:08:40,030
Come on.

425
01:09:50,640 --> 01:09:52,020
It's working.

426
01:09:59,610 --> 01:10:01,320
Come on.

427
01:11:17,520 --> 01:11:20,320
There's my father's plane. 
I trained on it.

428
01:11:31,370 --> 01:11:33,580
Yes! He made it.

429
01:11:35,540 --> 01:11:37,540
Get away from me.

430
01:11:40,040 --> 01:11:41,050
Leave!

431
01:11:42,800 --> 01:11:43,920
Now!

432
01:11:44,380 --> 01:11:45,550
Let's go!

433
01:11:50,510 --> 01:11:53,600
- The master's on. Throttle's set. 
- Come on. Let's go.

434
01:11:59,610 --> 01:12:02,650
Oh, please. You can't do this.

435
01:12:02,820 --> 01:12:04,440
I have no choice.

436
01:12:05,360 --> 01:12:07,700
The T-X...

437
01:12:07,990 --> 01:12:10,370
...has corrupted my system.

438
01:12:14,040 --> 01:12:17,040
You can't kill a human being. 
You said so yourself.

439
01:12:17,210 --> 01:12:19,080
Let him go!

440
01:12:23,760 --> 01:12:25,550
You're fighting it right now.

441
01:12:26,420 --> 01:12:28,510
My CPU is intact.

442
01:12:29,090 --> 01:12:32,890
But I cannot control my other functions.

443
01:12:33,060 --> 01:12:36,680
You don't have to do this. 
You don't want to do this!

444
01:12:37,190 --> 01:12:41,190
Desire is irrelevant.

445
01:12:41,400 --> 01:12:43,940
I am a machine.

446
01:13:00,540 --> 01:13:02,210
What is your mission?

447
01:13:03,960 --> 01:13:07,510
To ensure the survival of John Connor...

448
01:13:07,670 --> 01:13:09,720
...and Katherine Brewster.

449
01:13:15,060 --> 01:13:18,270
You are about to fail that mission!

450
01:13:25,150 --> 01:13:27,940
I can- I cannot.

451
01:13:29,030 --> 01:13:31,160
You know what you have to do.

452
01:13:33,120 --> 01:13:35,700
You know my destiny.

453
01:13:40,330 --> 01:13:41,500
I have to live.

454
01:14:22,210 --> 01:14:24,750
- Are you okay? 
- What happened?

455
01:14:24,920 --> 01:14:27,550
He couldn't do it. 
He shut himself down.

456
01:14:31,300 --> 01:14:33,890
- Can you fly? 
- Yeah.

457
01:15:01,290 --> 01:15:03,500
Okay. 015 degrees...

458
01:15:02,750 --> 01:15:07,880
...52 miles, our max air speed 
is about 160.

459
01:15:08,090 --> 01:15:10,460
We've got 32 minutes.

460
01:15:10,630 --> 01:15:12,470
It's just you and me now.

461
01:15:12,630 --> 01:15:15,090
What if we can't stop it?

462
01:15:15,720 --> 01:15:19,350
There's enough C-4 here 
to take out 10 supercomputers.

463
01:15:19,760 --> 01:15:22,100
We're gonna make it, Kate.

464
01:15:23,310 --> 01:15:25,690
The future is up to us.

465
01:15:32,110 --> 01:15:34,360
That's gotta be it.

466
01:16:37,510 --> 01:16:40,600
Skynet. There may be more of them.

467
01:16:45,770 --> 01:16:47,560
Come on.

468
01:17:01,780 --> 01:17:04,950
I think this is some kind of blast door.

469
01:17:08,080 --> 01:17:10,750
There's no way 
we can blow through this thing.

470
01:17:12,000 --> 01:17:13,000
John, look.

471
01:17:16,010 --> 01:17:17,420
Now what?

472
01:17:20,260 --> 01:17:22,600
It's a code prompt.

473
01:17:29,730 --> 01:17:32,770
Type in "Dakota 775."

474
01:17:37,030 --> 01:17:39,280
"Red 176."

475
01:18:00,300 --> 01:18:02,640
Come on! 
We gotta get this thing open.

476
01:18:02,890 --> 01:18:04,720
Here. It's "Avalon 412."

477
01:18:05,640 --> 01:18:06,970
Put it in!

478
01:18:41,340 --> 01:18:42,760
Come on!

479
01:18:58,360 --> 01:19:00,780
I'm back.

480
01:19:16,210 --> 01:19:18,380
Go! Now!

481
01:19:18,960 --> 01:19:19,960
Come on!

482
01:19:43,070 --> 01:19:45,400
- Thank you. 
- We'll meet again.

483
01:19:45,650 --> 01:19:46,820
Go!

484
01:19:47,990 --> 01:19:48,990
Come on!

485
01:20:31,990 --> 01:20:33,540
You are terminated.

486
01:21:04,150 --> 01:21:05,480
The elevator.

487
01:21:12,070 --> 01:21:14,490
I'll set the detonator for five minutes.

488
01:21:14,990 --> 01:21:17,410
That should give us enough time 
to get back up.

489
01:21:48,780 --> 01:21:50,530
What is this place?

490
01:22:31,240 --> 01:22:33,740
These computers are 30 years old.

491
01:22:42,250 --> 01:22:44,080
This isn't Skynet.

492
01:22:48,750 --> 01:22:50,590
There's nothing here.

493
01:22:55,760 --> 01:22:58,600
This is a fallout shelter for VIPs.

494
01:23:00,430 --> 01:23:02,770
Only they never got the warning.

495
01:23:17,070 --> 01:23:18,910
Why didn't he tell us?

496
01:23:22,250 --> 01:23:24,670
Why did he lead us down here?

497
01:23:30,420 --> 01:23:32,090
To live.

498
01:23:33,260 --> 01:23:35,260
That was his mission.

499
01:23:49,110 --> 01:23:50,360
There was never any stopping it.

500
01:23:54,950 --> 01:23:56,280
John...

501
01:23:57,610 --> 01:23:59,280
...we could just...

502
01:24:00,120 --> 01:24:01,450
...let it go.

503
01:24:04,290 --> 01:24:05,620
Hello?

504
01:24:06,420 --> 01:24:08,630
Hello? Can somebody hear me?

505
01:24:09,710 --> 01:24:11,550
This is Montana Civil Defense.

506
01:24:12,210 --> 01:24:15,300
Somebody please come in.

507
01:24:15,800 --> 01:24:17,470
Is there anybody there?

508
01:24:17,800 --> 01:24:20,800
Anyone reading me? Over.

509
01:24:21,970 --> 01:24:26,230
Rumors about a launch sequence. 
Command and control have broken down.

510
01:24:27,480 --> 01:24:30,560
Is anyone receiving me? 
Somebody?

511
01:24:32,650 --> 01:24:34,650
Somebody please come in.

512
01:24:35,070 --> 01:24:36,400
Anybody out there?

513
01:24:36,650 --> 01:24:39,990
- This is SAC Nellis. We're under attack. 
- CQ? CQ?

514
01:24:40,240 --> 01:24:41,830
Is anybody there?

515
01:24:43,830 --> 01:24:47,500
This is John Connor at Crystal Peak.

516
01:24:48,420 --> 01:24:53,170
Connor? What the hell is happening? 
Who's in charge there?

517
01:25:00,010 --> 01:25:01,350
I am.

518
01:25:02,680 --> 01:25:05,020
Connor, can you help us?

519
01:25:05,350 --> 01:25:10,190
This is Montana Civil Defense. 
Where did you say you were again?
